{{!-- One "labelled list of KEYED rows" on the Create-a-Site wizard: questions & answers, the
      timeline, denizens, and areas.

      The sibling of cs-line-list.hbs and here for the same reason — the block was pasted per list
      and differed only in wording. Everything outside the rows is cs-list-frame.hbs, shared
      between the two.

      Arity comes from the DATA, not from this file. An earlier cut took a fixed `keyA`/`keyB` pair
      of hash arguments, which meant it could serve only the two-key lists while SITE_PAIR_LISTS
      went on advertising areas' four — a list wired through it would have rendered its first two
      fields and silently dropped the rest, with the dropped ones still seeded, saved and shaped.
      So a row arrives as `cells`, one per key the schema declares, in the order it declares them
      (see _pairRows), and this file loops them.

      Two shapes, chosen per row:
        inline  every field on ONE control row (the timeline: a date and what happened read as a
                single line)
        else    the first field shares a row with the delete button and the rest stack under it,
                each cell either a single-line input or, if `multiline`, a textarea

      Every cell carries its own `list` and `index` rather than being walked back to with `../`:
      inside a partial's block the hash arguments have pushed a frame, so the depth a `../` chain
      lands on depends on how the partial was called, and getting it wrong fails by reading
      undefined — a `data-list=""` that no delegated handler matches.

      Context: the frame's, plus
        rows  this list's rows ({index, list, rowClass, inline, cells}), each cell
              {list, index, key, first, value, placeholder, cls, multiline, lines} --}}
{{#> "stonetop.cs-list-frame" list=list label=label hint=hint chips=chips kinds=kinds addLabel=addLabel frameClass=frameClass}}
  {{#each rows}}
  {{#if inline}}
  <div class="stonetop-cf-gear-row">
    {{#each cells}}
    <input type="text" class="stonetop-cf-input stonetop-cs-pair {{cls}}" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{key}}" value="{{value}}" placeholder="{{placeholder}}">
    {{/each}}
    <button type="button" class="stonetop-cs-remove stonetop-cf-mini-btn stonetop-cf-mini-btn--danger" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}"><i class="fas fa-times"></i></button>
  </div>
  {{else}}
  <div class="{{rowClass}}">
    {{#each cells}}
    {{#if first}}
    <div class="stonetop-cf-gear-row">
      <input type="text" class="stonetop-cf-input stonetop-cs-pair {{cls}}" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{key}}" value="{{value}}" placeholder="{{placeholder}}">
      <button type="button" class="stonetop-cs-remove stonetop-cf-mini-btn stonetop-cf-mini-btn--danger" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}"><i class="fas fa-times"></i></button>
    </div>
    {{else if multiline}}
    <textarea class="stonetop-cf-textarea stonetop-cs-pair {{cls}}" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{key}}" rows="{{lines}}" placeholder="{{placeholder}}">{{value}}</textarea>
    {{else}}
    <input type="text" class="stonetop-cf-input stonetop-cs-pair {{cls}}" data-list="{{list}}" data-index="{{index}}" data-key="{{key}}" value="{{value}}" placeholder="{{placeholder}}">
    {{/if}}
    {{/each}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}
  {{/each}}
{{/"stonetop.cs-list-frame"}}
